  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The FIGS Club - Educating Tomorrow&apos;s Scientists</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Future Indigenous Guardians of Science (FIGS) Club is an afterschool science and environmental education program for the youth of Wanang Conservation Area (WCA). 20 years ago WCA turned to conservation after rejecting loggers. Since then research at WCA has brought sustainable development for the whole village. Each year the FIGS Club will lay the foundations for 30 Wanang youth to pursue careers as local research assistants and conservationists bringing personal and community development.</narrative>
  </description>
